|               4.161               |    15.556     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -8577.06, AIC-c = 17254.63 (50 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0697
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   1.0076
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.000               |    51.290     |                                   |
|               1.452               |    41.759     |                                   |
|               5.665               |     6.951     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -8573.25, AIC-c = 17249.03 (51 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0708
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.7126
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   1.1225
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   1.1225
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.000               |    51.228     |                                   |
|               1.491               |    43.147     |                                   |
|               6.344               |     5.625     |                                   |


